<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Events>
<!--
  Windows event log entries to collect (VCF Content Factory vCommunity).

  This list matters only if the account's Windows Event Log Monitoring
  Status is Enabled. This file is not a comma list. The root element is
  Events. Inside it, one Log
  element per Windows event log names the log in its Name attribute, and holds
  one EventID element per event number to report, each a whole number.
  Anything else (another element, a Log without a Name, an EventID that is not
  a whole number) makes the whole file unusable, and the last good list stays
  in force.

  Do not edit this shipped file: a forced upgrade of the pack replaces it and
  your edits are lost. Make a copy under another name in the VCF Operations
  configuration-file store, and enter that name (no .xml) in the account's
  Windows Event Log Configuration File field. As shipped, no Log is switched on, so no event is collected.
  To switch one on, copy it out of this comment into the Events element.

  Examples, one Log per block:

  <Log Name="System">
    <EventID>41</EventID>
    <EventID>6008</EventID>
  </Log>

  <Log Name="Application">
    <EventID>1002</EventID>
  </Log>
-->
</Events>
